-- title:
--   Inertia-invariant prime-to-p torsion of J₁(Mp) bounded by its finite part
-- statement:
--   The statement is set up in a fixed frame for the curve $X_1(Mp)$ at the prime $p$, and its conclusion is a comparison of two cardinalities of subsets of $J_1(Mp)$.
--
--   **Arithmetic base data.** A prime $p$, an integer $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$ (and $M \neq 0$), a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Next, $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ subject to `hK`, which requires $K$ to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Further, $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAp`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$; finally $j \in K$ is a nonzero element whose Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant under the coefficient embedding $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ (`hj`).
--
--   **The two-chart model and its special fibre.** [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) is the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ of the scheme obtained by gluing the spectra of the two chart subalgebras `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` and `chartAlgInf A ↥K j` of $K$; it is assumed proper. Over an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra, two schemes $C_1, C_2$ are given with morphisms $c_1, c_2$ to $\operatorname{Spec} k$ that are proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, together with closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of $C_1, C_2$ into the base change of the two-chart model to $k$, compatible with the structure morphisms. The hypothesis `hcover` requires every point of that base change to lie in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; `hred` requires the scheme-theoretic intersection $\mathrm{pullback}\,i_1\,i_2$ to be reduced; and `hn`, `hn0` fix a positive natural number $n$ equal to the number of points of that intersection.
--
--   **Sections.** A section $\varepsilon$ of the two-chart model over $A$, sections $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ of $c_1, c_2$, and `hε₁`: $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ is the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $k$.
--
--   **Relative Picard data.** $D$ is a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation for the two-chart model over $A$, that is, a scheme $D.P$ with a morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section; `hrep` asserts that the type of data exhibiting $D$ as representing the subfunctor of the rigidified relative Picard functor cut out by fibrewise algebraic triviality (`algEquivZeroCut`) is nonempty, and `hsm`, `hsep` require $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to be smooth and separated. The hypothesis `hreps` is such a representability datum for the base change of the curve and of $D$ to $k$, and `hPk` requires the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` to be isomorphic to the base change to $k$ (via `BaseChange.ofR`) of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some` along the first projection of $D.P \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} k$. Likewise $D_1, D_2$ are relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designations for $c_1, c_2$ with nonempty representability data `hrep₁`, `hrep₂`.
--
--   **Restriction to the second component.** A morphism $\nu_2$ from $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$ to $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $k$, subject to `hν₂`: for every $k$-scheme $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and every $T$-point $a$ of $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂.some` along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the rigidification along the section $\varepsilon_2$ (in the sense of `Scheme.Modules.rigidify`) of the pullback along `curveChange i₂.1` of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` along $a$. Thus $\nu_2$ implements restriction of line bundles to $C_2$.
--
--   **The geometric generic fibre.** Compatible algebra structures of $A$ and $L$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ are fixed. Then $M\eta$ is a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) (a proper smooth integral curve with a prescribed isomorphism of its function field with that field and a bijection from its closed points to the places), $e\eta$ is an isomorphism from $M\eta.C$ to the base change of the two-chart model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $e\eta$ followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equal to $M\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ (`heη`). The instance `Mη_chart_nonempty` requires the preimage under $e\eta$ followed by the first projection of the image of the finite chart to be a nonempty open subscheme, and `hMηpin` requires, for every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, that the function-field element obtained by transporting the germ of $a$ at the generic point through $M\eta.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ has Laurent series equal to the coefficientwise image under $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the Laurent series of $a$.
--
--   **Galois equivariance.** The hypothesis `hgal` requires, for every $g \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing $L$ pointwise and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M\eta.C$ (sections of $M\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$): if $x'$ followed by $e\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by $x$ followed by $e\eta$ and the first projection, then the place $M\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x'$ is the translate of $M\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x$ by the semilinear automorphism [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)) g`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) attached to $g$.
--
--   **Special-fibre group bookkeeping.** $G$ is a [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9), i.e. abelian groups $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$ with a distinguished subgroup $G.\mathrm{torus} \le G.J0s$ and a surjective homomorphism $G.\mathrm{proj} : G.J0s \to G.JI \times G.JE$ with kernel $G.\mathrm{torus}$. Bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` identify $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$ with the sets of $k$-points of $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_1.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$; the hypotheses `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` require each bijection to be additive in the sense that the pullback of the relevant Poincaré bundle along the point attached to a sum is isomorphic to the tensor product of the pullbacks along the two summands; and `hproj` requires, for every $x \in G.J0s$, that `ptsI` of the first component of $G.\mathrm{proj}\,x$ is `pts x` followed by the morphism `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom i₁.1 i₁.2 hε₁ hreps hrep₁.some`, and that `ptsE` of the second component is `pts x` followed by $\nu_2$.
--
--   **Igusa models of the components.** $w$ is an [`ModularCurve.IntegralWeightOneForm k M`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L16), consisting of a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$, an integral power series realising its $q$-expansion, and the requirement that the reduction of that series in $k$ be nonzero. Then $Mdl_1$, $Mdl_2$ are curve models over $k$ of the Igusa function field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), with isomorphisms $e_1 : Mdl_1.C \cong C_1$ and $e_2 : Mdl_2.C \cong C_2$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`he₁`, `he₂`).
--
--   **The dictionary `gpts` and the Abel–Jacobi pinning.** `gpts` is a bijection from $J_1(Mp) = \mathrm{Pic}^0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}, \mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp))$ to the set of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $A$, additive for the relative group law supplied by `hrep.some` on the designation cut out by `algEquivZeroGroupCut` (`hgadd`). Over $L$, `hDL` is a representability datum for the base change to $L$, `ajL` is a morphism over $L$ from the base-changed curve to $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L).\mathrm{toBase}$, `kL` a morphism between the base changes to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and to $L$, `ajbar` a morphism $M\eta.C \to D.P$ and `εbar` a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $M\eta.C$. These are pinned by: `hPL` (the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` is isomorphic to the base change to $L$ of the pullback of that of `hrep.some` along the first projection); `hajLε` ($\varepsilon$ base-changed to $L$ followed by `ajL` is the zero section); `hajL` (for every field $K'$, every morphism $t : \operatorname{Spec} K' \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ and every $K'$-point $x$ of the curve over $L$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` along $x$ followed by `ajL` is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of the point $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of the section $t$ followed by $\varepsilon_L$ — so `ajL` is the Abel–Jacobi map $x \mapsto [x - \varepsilon]$); `hkL₁`, `hkL₂` (compatibility of `kL` with both projections, the second up to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$); `hajbar` (`ajbar` is $e\eta$ followed by `kL`, `ajL` and the first projection) and `hajbar_over` (its compatibility over the base); `hεbar` and `hεbar_aj` (`εbar` is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point induced by $\varepsilon$, and composing it with `ajbar` gives the zero section); and `hpts_aj`: for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M\eta.C$ with $s$ inducing $\varepsilon$, there is a degree-zero divisor $Dv$ on $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ equal to the difference of the places of $x$ and of $s$, such that the point `gpts` of the class of $Dv$ is $x$ followed by `ajbar`.
--
--   **The place above $p$.** $Pl$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `Pl.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. $p$ is a nonunit of $Pl$; $\rho : A \to Pl$ is a ring homomorphism whose composition with the inclusion $Pl \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map $A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hρ`); and $\pi_k : Pl \to k$ is a surjective ring homomorphism with $\pi_k \circ \rho$ equal to the structure map $A \to k$ (`hAlgk`, `hπk`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a natural number $C$ such that $0 < C$ and such that for every natural number $n'$ with $0 < n'$ and $p \nmid n'$,
--   $$\#\,S_{\mathrm{inv}}(n') \le C \cdot \#\,S_{\mathrm{fin}}(n'),$$
--   both cardinalities taken as `Nat.card`, where $S_{\mathrm{inv}}(n')$ is the set of $x \in J_1(Mp)$ that lie in [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.torsion`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L244) for $n'$ (that is, $n'x = 0$) and satisfy $\sigma \bullet x = x$ for every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ belonging to `Pl.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image of the inertia subgroup of $Pl$ under the inclusion of its decomposition subgroup) that fixes $L$ pointwise; and $S_{\mathrm{fin}}(n')$ is the set of $x \in J_1(Mp)$ with $n'x = 0$ for which there exists a point $z$ of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho)$ with source $\operatorname{Spec} Pl$ such that $(\mathrm{gpts}\,x).1$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $Pl \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $z$, i.e. the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point attached to $x$ extends to a $Pl$-point of $D$.
--
--   This is the quantitative input of Néron-model type in the analysis of $J_1(Mp)$ at $p$: the prime-to-$p$ torsion invariant under the inertia at a place above $p$ fixing $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ exceeds the part extending to a $Pl$-integral point of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the two-chart model only by a bounded factor, the bound being uniform in the torsion order $n'$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_forall_exists_eq_smul_sub_of_proj_eq_zero_of_points_valuationSubring_of_curveModel_igusa_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_forall_exists_eq_smul_sub_of_proj_eq_zero_of_points_valuationSubring_of_curveModel_igusa_twoChartModel_x1_mul), and rests on [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_points_valuationSubring_nsmul_of_forall_smul_eq_self_of_curveModel_igusa_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_points_valuationSubring_nsmul_of_forall_smul_eq_self_of_curveModel_igusa_twoChartModel_x1_mul) together with the finiteness of the torsion of $J_1$ recorded in [`ModularCurve.finite_torsion_jOne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finite_torsion_jOne).
